<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Matches api/Biolog.Api/Biolog.Api.csproj's pinned TFM (BIO-FND-008), same as BIO-BIO-001/002/003. -->
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    No ASP.NET Core dependency, no NuGet package references. This project DOES reference
    BIO-BIO-001's provider-neutral biometric library directly - a feature-to-feature
    ProjectReference, not a shared/common one - because 1:1 verification reuses BIO-BIO-001's own
    IBiometricTemplateStore/IFingerprintProvider/IBiometricMatcher seams exactly as
    Service.BiometricService.VerifyAsync already established them (BIO-BIO-001-AC03), rather than
    re-deriving an equivalent contract. Same accepted shape as BIO-BIO-002/003/BIO-DOC-002/003
    referencing their own foundation library directly.

    The approved story also names BIO-BIO-002 (guided tenprint/single-finger enrolment) as a
    dependency, but deliberately NO ProjectReference exists to it here: BIO-BIO-002's own
    IFingerprintEnrolmentRepository/FingerprintEnrolmentService are internal, Singleton-registered,
    and expose no "resolve by claimed identity" query at all (only get-by-session-id) - captured
    fingerprint templates live embedded in its own FingerprintEnrolmentSession aggregate, never
    published to BIO-BIO-001's IBiometricTemplateStore. Reaching into BIO-BIO-002's owned paths to
    add such a query is out of this story's write scope (governance/feature-path-ownership.json
    grants this story only api|web|mobile|tests|docs|evidence/features/bio-bio-004/**). This
    story instead verifies against BIO-BIO-001's own IBiometricTemplateStore - the SAME seam
    BiometricService.EnrollAsync/VerifyAsync already define for exactly this purpose - and
    documents the BIO-BIO-002-does-not-populate-that-store gap explicitly rather than silently
    working around it (see docs/features/bio-bio-004/README.md "Design decisions").

    Deliberately NO ProjectReference to BIO-IDN-001 either (AC04's suspended/revoked gate):
    PersonRegistry's PersonService is a tenant-scoped, Scoped-registered aggregate service (the
    same shape BIO-PHO-001/BIO-BIO-003 already document for why THEY have no direct
    ProjectReference to their own upstream dependency). This project defines its own narrow
    Domain/IIdentityStatusGateway.cs instead; the real implementation is an adapter in
    Biolog.Api.Modules.BioBio004Module wrapping BIO-IDN-001's already-registered
    PersonService.GetAsync, the identical pattern BioIdn002-006Module/BioPho001-002Module/
    BioBio003Module already use for their own read-only gateways.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../../bio-bio-001/Biolog.Features.Biometrics/Biolog.Features.Biometrics.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- IFingerprintVerificationRecordStore/InMemoryFingerprintVerificationRecordStore and
         FingerprintVerificationService are internal (BIO-IDN-001-QA-01's governance shape,
         mirrored by BIO-BIO-002/003). This is the explicit, auditable seam that grants
         Biolog.Api (DI registration in Modules/BioBio004Module.cs) and this feature's own test
         project the same access. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Api" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Features.FingerprintVerification.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
